title: 6. Jeff is asked only what is to be built and what cannot be undone; the rest the team decides, and writes down where he can reverse it.
pid: bf96bac6-0731-4694-9cb0-103a25be6b3b
body: |2-
  A one-way door goes to him even when Tay is sure of the answer; a
  two-way door does not, even when the author is unsure. A
  disagreement between Tay and the author that survives the readings
  goes to him at once. Top asks, one question per headline, with the
  recommended answer and the default; work that does not wait on an
  answer goes ahead.
  Why, and its sources: [[id:13202324-4cca-4ffd-8fea-a6dcbdaa15fd][step 6, its reasons]].
